<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Beacon digest fires. Install + load with:
       cp deploy/com.beacon.digest.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
       launchctl bootout  gui/$UID/com.beacon.digest 2>/dev/null
       launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.beacon.digest.plist

     One fire a day — 16:00 local time (Asia/Jakarta on this box; launchd reads the system
     zone, which is also config.LOCAL_TZ). The fire polls the sources and pushes the Telegram
     digest, then exits: no RunAtLoad, no KeepAlive, nothing to kill.
     deploy/hourly-digest.sh holds the lock and watchdog that cap a run.

     Why one: narrowed from three fires (08:00/12:00/16:30) on 2026-09-30 at the user's
     request — one digest a day, late afternoon. A full poll runs ~13 min concurrent (slice 27;
     29 min sequential) against a 50 min watchdog, so a fire can never meet the next one. Nothing
     is lost to a skipped or killed run either way: application/notify.py writes seen_matches
     only AFTER the notifier succeeds, so unnotified matches roll into the next digest.

     A LaunchAgent lives in the user's GUI domain, so it only fires while logged in, and a
     sleeping Mac is not woken. launchd runs a missed fire once on login/wake (they coalesce),
     so waking the Mac at 16:20 gets the 16:00 fire at 16:20.
     `sudo pmset repeat wakeorpoweron MTWRFSU 15:59:00` if it must be guaranteed.

     TCC: keep the checkout OUT of ~/Documents, ~/Desktop and ~/Downloads. A launchd-started
     job has no access there and dies before it starts — `Operation not permitted`, exit 126
     (proved 2026-09-10; hand-runs still work, because the terminal holds the grant). The move
     to ~/Projects/beacon is confirmed good: the 2026-09-11 09:30 fire ran the script.

     Paths are absolute because launchd has no working shell. Telegram creds are read from
     app_settings in beacon.db (Settings UI) and every path in Settings resolves from the repo
     root, so no BEACON_* env is needed here. Moving the checkout means editing this file.
     Tail logs at /tmp/beacon.digest.{out,err}.log. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.beacon.digest</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/tomtomtomtom/Projects/beacon/deploy/hourly-digest.sh</string>
    </array>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/tomtomtomtom/Projects/beacon</string>
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>16</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
    </array>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/beacon.digest.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/beacon.digest.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
